{"name":"Signal","hex":"#cc0002","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"signal","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sequence of states representing an encoded message in a communication channel.","Any variation of a quantity or change in an entity over time that conveys information upon detection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To indicate; to convey or communicate by a signal.","To communicate with (a person or system) by a signal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/signal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Signal","blocks":[{"text":"A signal is both the process and the result of transmission of data over some media accomplished by embedding some variation. Signals are important in multiple subject fields, including signal processing, information theory and biology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/William_Powell_Frith_The_signal_1858.jpg/330px-William_Powell_Frith_The_signal_1858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Signal","wikidata":"Q174984"},{"title":"Signal (software)","blocks":[{"text":"Signal is an open-source, encrypted messaging service for instant messaging, voice calls, and video calls. The instant messaging function includes sending text, voice notes, images, videos, and other files. Communication may be one-to-one between users or may involve group messaging."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Signal-Logo-Ultramarine_%282024%29.svg/330px-Signal-Logo-Ultramarine_%282024%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Signal_(software)","wikidata":"Q19718090"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Signal_processing_system.png/500px-Signal_processing_system.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w